# November 20, 2026: a first scatter of places across South Carolina, outside Beaufort County (which sc_vxwi covered):
# the Upstate (Greenville, Pickens, Oconee, Union), the Midlands (Columbia, Camden, Ninety Six, Aiken County), the
# Pee Dee (Cheraw) and the Lowcountry north of Charleston (Berkeley, Dorchester, Georgetown and Charleston counties).
# Region sc claimed with choose.py --thinnest (the state then had 16 places, the fewest of any).
# Facts come only from sources opened in this session: Wikipedia read as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py), the National
# Register nomination for St. David's, Cheraw (NPGallery text), the pages of South Carolina State Parks, the National
# Park Service, SCDNR (Poinsett Bridge news, June 2024), the City of Columbia's parks page, Old Santee Canal Park,
# Historic Camden and Prince George Winyah Parish. Where a manager's page could not be read the access note says so.
from data_b import N
